{"title":"Career roadmap · Textile Quality Controller","role":"Textile Quality Controller","summary":"A Textile Quality Controller ensures that fibres, yarns, fabrics, garments, dyes, finishes, and finished textile products meet defined quality, performance, colour, dimensional, safety, and customer specifications.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Textile Engineering / Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is a directly aligned career for Textile Engineering / Technology graduates."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical quality flow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Raw Material","Spinning","Weaving/Knitting","Dyeing","Processing","Finishing","Inspection","Testing","Packing","Dispatch"]},{"type":"h","text":"Career-route check"},{"type":"note","label":"Starts","text":"Year 1 of B.Tech/B.E."},{"type":"note","label":"Current degree","text":"B.Tech / B.E. Textile Engineering / Technology"},{"type":"note","label":"Desired career","text":"Textile Quality Controller"},{"type":"flow","items":["Textile Manufacturing","Quality Control","Textile Testing","Quality Assurance"],"label":"Career cluster"},{"type":"note","label":"Entry accessibility","text":"Direct"},{"type":"note","label":"Typical entry titles","text":"Quality Trainee, QC Executive, Textile Quality Executive, Quality Inspector, Lab Technician, Textile Testing Executive, Graduate Engineer Trainee"},{"type":"note","label":"Assumption","text":"four-year B.Tech/B.E. beginning in 2026, graduating around 2030."}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career direction"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build textile materials, manufacturing, testing, inspection, statistics and quality-system fundamentals."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Enter textile QC/QA and specialise in fabric, yarn, garment, dyeing/processing or textile testing."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Move toward Senior Quality Engineer, Quality Lead, Quality Manager, Testing Specialist or Supplier Quality."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Progress toward Quality Head, Technical Quality Manager, Textile Testing Laboratory leadership, Sustainability/Compliance Quality or Global Supplier Quality."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Textile fibres, engineering mathematics, chemistry, basic manufacturing"},{"text":"NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Fibre identification mini-project"},{"text":"Textile fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Natural/synthetic fibres, yarn formation, textile properties"},{"text":"NPTEL + laboratory work"},{"text":"Fibre/yarn testing report"},{"text":"Materials knowledge"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Spinning, yarn manufacturing, yarn quality"},{"text":"NPTEL + textile labs"},{"text":"Yarn quality analysis"},{"text":"Process understanding"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Weaving, knitting, fabric construction and defects"},{"text":"NPTEL + mill exposure"},{"text":"Fabric defect catalogue"},{"text":"Fabric knowledge"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Dyeing, printing, finishing and textile chemical processing"},{"text":"NPTEL + laboratory"},{"text":"Colour/finish evaluation project"},{"text":"Processing quality"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Textile testing, statistics, QC tools, quality systems"},{"text":"NPTEL + ASQ","url":"https://asq.org/"},{"text":"SPC/control-chart project"},{"text":"Quality engineering"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"QA/QC systems, inspection, root-cause analysis, audits"},{"text":"Industry internship + standards"},{"text":"Complete quality-improvement case study"},{"text":"Industrial readiness"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Capstone + textile QC internship + placement preparation"},{"text":"Industry + NPTEL"},{"text":"Production-quality project + internship"},{"text":"Job readiness"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Core technical subjects"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Textile Fibre Science"},{"text":"Yarn Manufacturing"},{"text":"Spinning Technology"},{"text":"Weaving Technology"},{"text":"Knitting Technology"},{"text":"Textile Chemical Processing"},{"text":"Dyeing"},{"text":"Printing"},{"text":"Finishing"},{"text":"Textile Testing"},{"text":"Fabric Structure"},{"text":"Textile Physics"},{"text":"Textile Chemistry"},{"text":"Apparel Technology"},{"text":"Textile Machinery"},{"text":"Industrial Engineering"},{"text":"Production Management"},{"text":"Quality Control"},{"text":"Quality Assurance"},{"text":"Statistics and Probability"},{"text":"Operations Research"},{"text":"Industrial Safety"},{"text":"Environmental Management"},{"text":"Sustainable Textiles"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important laboratory skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to work with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fibre identification"},{"text":"Fibre fineness and strength"},{"text":"Yarn count"},{"text":"Yarn twist"},{"text":"Yarn tensile strength"},{"text":"Yarn unevenness"},{"text":"Fabric GSM"},{"text":"Fabric thickness"},{"text":"Tensile strength"},{"text":"Tear strength"},{"text":"Bursting strength"},{"text":"Abrasion resistance"},{"text":"Pilling resistance"},{"text":"Shrinkage"},{"text":"Colour fastness"},{"text":"Dimensional stability"},{"text":"Moisture regain"},{"text":"Fabric defect inspection"},{"text":"Colour measurement"},{"text":"Spectrophotometer"},{"text":"Microscopy"},{"text":"Moisture testing"},{"text":"Statistical quality analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Quality tools to master"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"7 QC tools"},{"text":"Pareto analysis"},{"text":"Fishbone/Ishikawa"},{"text":"5 Whys"},{"text":"Control charts"},{"text":"SPC"},{"text":"Sampling plans"},{"text":"AQL"},{"text":"CAPA"},{"text":"Root Cause Analysis"},{"